---
import SectionHead from '../SectionHead.astro';
---

<section id="bridge" aria-label="Why case studies underperform">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="col-prose">
        <SectionHead title="Why are most B2B case studies <em>underperforming</em>?" />
        <div class="prose-body">
          <p>Most case studies were designed for a buying journey that ran through a sales rep. That journey is gone.</p>
          <p><em>63% of B2B buyers now shortlist two or three vendors before sales ever hears their name.</em> They start on Google. They ask ChatGPT for examples. They scan the page for 45 seconds and decide whether to keep reading.</p>
          <p>The case study itself hasn't changed. Same length, same shape, same anonymous quotes. It's the channels that changed, and the format never caught up.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-diag">
        <h3>Are any of these true of your case studies?</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>They take longer to produce than you'd like.</li>
          <li>Your team finishes drafts but the final piece never quite gets shipped.</li>
          <li>Quotes are anonymous, partial, or undated.</li>
          <li>Metrics aren't attached to a named person at a named company.</li>
          <li>Searching "[your category] case study" on Google doesn't surface them.</li>
          <li>Asking ChatGPT for examples in your category doesn't surface them either.</li>
          <li>You can't remember the last time sales mentioned a case study by name.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="closing">If any apply, the Citable Case Study format will fix the structural problems behind them. If none apply, you probably don't need us.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  section {
    padding: 120px 0;
    background: var(--yellow);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .two-col {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 80px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .col-prose :global(.sec-head) {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }
  .col-prose :global(.sec-head h2) {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 56px);
  }
  .prose-body {
    margin-top: 48px;
  }
  .prose-body p {
    font-size: 21px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 24px;
  }
  .prose-body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .prose-body p :global(em) {
    font-style: italic;
  }
  h3 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.5vw, 36px);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 32px;
  }
  ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 32px;
  }
  li {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink);
    padding: 12px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  li:first-child {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  li::before {
    content: '—';
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .closing {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .two-col {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 48px;
    }
  }
</style>
